# Versioning rules

Human-readable guide: **`docs/versioning.md`**.

## Hard rule — PR `.ver` files live at `version/entries/` root, never under `preproduction */` by hand

- **Author new or revised release rows for a feature PR only as** **`version/entries/*.ver`** (the file’s parent directory must be **`version/entries/`** itself, **not** **`version/entries/preproduction <A>.<B>.<C>/`**).
- **`version/entries/preproduction <A>.<B>.<C>/`** is **not** where Cursor/AI or same-repo humans add PR prose: **`./scripts/relocate_root_prerelease_ver_to_preproduction.sh`** and the **GitHub Actions** versioning / **Version lock** steps **move** root **`PRERELEASE=1`** **`.ver`** files **into** that directory after optional **`RELEASE_DATE`** stamping. **Do not** commit new `.ver` paths there to “save a step”—commit at the **entries root** and let automation relocate.
- **Omit `RELEASE_DATE=`** on new root rows unless a maintainer workflow says otherwise; relocate / merge automation stamps dates per **`docs/versioning.md`**.

## Lock system — never rewrite shipped published files

- **Do not** modify paths under **`version/locked/`** that are already present on the **target / merge-base** branch. After merge, those files are the **published** record. New release prose belongs in **`version/entries/`** only on normal feature work; **`version/locked/`** is refreshed by **Version lock on merge** (GitHub Actions) after changes land on **`develop`** (see **AI / Cursor agent PRs** below).
- **Before merge:** **`version/entries/*.ver`** files that exist **only** on your feature branch may be edited or removed freely.
- **`version/entries/`** is where **`.ver`** files are authored and revised. **`version/locked/`** is the **published snapshot** (full copy of **`version/entries/`** when finalize / automation runs). Until then, **`version/entries/`** may contain **additional** files not yet in **`version/locked/`**.
- **`userland/shell/version_def.h`** is **generated** from the highest triple in **`version/locked/**/*.ver`** plus **`VERSION_LINE`** from **`version/entries/**/*.ver`** when **`PRERELEASE=1`** exists (`scripts/gen_version_def.sh`). Treat the committed header on **`develop`** as **published**; do not hand-edit **`VERSION_*`**. **Cursor / AI on same-repo feature PRs:** do **not** commit this header (**`make`** may refresh it locally—leave it unstaged). Prerelease **`.ver`** files use **`PRERELEASE`**, optional **`PRERELEASE_TAG`**, **`GM`**, and **`DEV_VERSION`** (see **`docs/versioning.md`**); on same-repo branches **author** **`PRERELEASE=1`** rows at **`version/entries/`** root and let CI relocate them into **`preproduction */`**. **`main`** must not retain **`PRERELEASE=1`**, **`GM=1`**, **`DEV_VERSION=`**, or **`preproduction *`** paths.
- **CI** enforces **`version/locked`** immutability on PRs (`check_version_locked_immutable.sh`; **`version/locked/ABOUT.txt`** is excluded as non-release prose) and requires every **`version/locked`** file to **byte-match** the same path under **`version/entries/`** (`check_version_locked_subset_of_entries.sh`).
- **AI edits** must **skip** historical **`version/locked/**`** from bulk refactors.

## AI / Cursor agent PRs — `version/entries` only

- On **Cursor- and AI-authored pull requests**, add or revise **`version/entries/*.ver`** for the release you are shipping in that PR.
- **Do not** commit changes under **`version/locked/**`**. Those paths are the **published** record on **`develop`**; **Version lock on merge** (GitHub Actions on push to **`develop`**) runs **`relocate_root_prerelease_ver_to_preproduction.sh`**, **`finalize_version_locked.sh`**, **`stamp_version_release_date.sh`** when applicable, and **`gen_version_def.sh`**, then opens a PR to publish updates when needed. **Do not** commit **`userland/shell/version_def.h`** on same-repo feature PRs—**CI** may relocate root **`PRERELEASE=1`** rows, run **`gen_version_def.sh`**, and **push** one commit for **`version/entries`** + the header when needed. **AI:** never **`git add`** the header after local **`make`**. **`DEV_VERSION`:** vs **`develop`**, set **`DEV_VERSION`** to exactly **`N+1`** at most once per **`.ver`** (**`N`** on **`develop`** or **`0`**); **never** edit **`DEV_VERSION`** again after that—including **raising** it mid-branch (for example **8→9**); use **`DESCRIPTION`** only. **Never** set **`GM=1`** without **explicit human maintainer** permission. Regenerate locally only for fork PRs or offline **`check_version_header_matches_locked`** when not waiting for the bot commit.
- **`version/entries/ABOUT.txt`** must **byte-match** **`version/locked/ABOUT.txt`** while **`version/locked/`** is unchanged from the merge target (`check_version_locked_subset_of_entries.sh`). If you are not updating locked in the PR, reset **`version/entries/ABOUT.txt`** to match the target’s **`version/locked/ABOUT.txt`** (or leave it unchanged from the target).
- **Maintainers** may run **`./scripts/finalize_version_locked.sh`** / **`make finalize-version-locked`** locally before merge for an early snapshot on the branch; that is **not** the default agent workflow.

## Agent workflow — preproduction version (directories), iteration, and no semver backtracking

- On the **first** substantive code change for a pull request, **add** **`version/entries/*.ver`** at the **`version/entries/`** root if the branch does not already have an entry that covers **that** PR (for **`PRERELEASE=1`**, **do not** hand-add new **`.ver`** under **`preproduction A.B.C/`** on same-repo branches—CI relocates from the root). **AI:** new **`.ver`** files go in **`version/entries/`**, not in **`preproduction <A>.<B>.<C>/`** one level lower; not under **`version/locked/`**; omit **`RELEASE_DATE=`** (Actions dates on relocate / Version lock); Actions moves root **`PRERELEASE=1`** rows into **`preproduction <A>.<B>.<C>/`**. Do not edit **`RELEASE_DATE`** on existing preproduction rows.
- **Do not backtrack shipped semver for AI-authored work:** the **preproduction version** is **A.B.C** from the directory **`version/entries/preproduction <A>.<B>.<C>/`** (**`PRERELEASE=1`** rows land there **after** relocate). Do **not** add a **new root** **`version/entries/*.ver`** whose **A.B.C** is **numerically below** that **A.B.C** unless a **human maintainer** explicitly requests that separate GA release. **Default (AI / same-repo PRs):** add **another** root **`PRERELEASE=1`** **`*.ver`** with the same semver for a **new** PR train, or follow maintainer policy for **`DEV_VERSION`**; **never** set **`GM=1`** without **explicit human maintainer** permission; **`DEV_VERSION`** on a **`.ver`** you own follows **`N+1`**-once vs **`develop`** (see **AI / Cursor agent PRs** above). **Do not** edit **`DESCRIPTION`** / **`DEV_VERSION`** on **`.ver`** already under **`preproduction */`** that belong to a **different** PR's train—those are relocated snapshots. Relocate moves each new root row into that folder; **`promote_preproduction_for_main.sh`** (after **`GM=1`**) writes one GA root **`.ver`** using **only** the **`GM=1`** file’s **`DESCRIPTION`** and semver, then deletes the whole **`preproduction */`** tree from **`version/entries`**.
- For **one** conventional GA feature at **`version/entries/`** root (no **`preproduction */`**), **one** **`.ver`** revised in place is often enough across the whole PR.

## `.ver` filename convention (AI / authors)

- Prefer **`A_B_C_short_slug.ver`** (three semver components, underscore-separated, then a short slug). Example: **`3_2_0_shell_history_disk_cursor.ver`**.
- Avoid optional **`NNN_`** numeric serial prefixes unless you are matching an existing legacy pattern (e.g. **`001_2_2_4_baseline.ver`**). **Ordering is defined only by the `MAJOR_VERSION` / `STANDARD_VERSION` / `RELEASE_VERSION` fields inside the file**, not by the filename prefix.

## Canonical version & changelog

- **`userland/shell/version_def.h`** — **Generated** by **`scripts/gen_version_def.sh`** (also from **`make`**). **`VERSION`** = **A.B.C** from the **highest** triple in **`version/locked/*.ver`**; **`VERSION_LINE`** adds prerelease display from **`version/entries/**/*.ver`** when **`PRERELEASE=1`**. CI ensures the committed header matches the generator output for the branch’s **`version/locked/`** tree and **`version/entries/**/*.ver`**.
- **`version/entries/`** — author **`.ver`** release notes here (agents: **commit entries only**; see above).
- **`version/locked/`** — **published** snapshot; updated by automation (and optionally by maintainers running finalize), not by default agent commits.
- **GitHub Actions:** **`scripts/gen_version_changelog.c`** reads **`version/locked`**, then **`make CHANGELOG_CI=1`** (see `.github/workflows/c-cpp.yml`).
- **`scripts/export_version_record.sh`** — prints keys / JSON from `version_def.h` for deployment pipelines.
- Use **semantic versioning**: **`A.B.C`**.

## Semver meanings

| Component | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| **A** | Major — architecture or milestone-level overhauls, incompatible or foundational changes |
| **B** | Minor — new features (additive behavior) |
| **C** | Patch — bug fixes and small, localized corrections |

### Bump precedence (`A` > `B` > `C`)

**Precedence (importance):** **`A` > `B` > `C`**. When you record a new release, choose **one** bump level: the **highest** precedence that applies to that release as a whole.

- **Increment** only that component (the most significant level that changed for this release).
- **Leave unchanged** every component **more significant** than the one you bumped (to the **left** in `A.B.C`).
- **Set to `0`** every component **less significant** than the one you bumped (to the **right** in `A.B.C`).

So a **minor** bump from **`2.2.4`** is **`2.3.0`**: **`A`** stays `2`, **`B`** becomes `3`, **`C`** resets to **`0`** (not `2.3.4`). A **major** bump from **`2.3.7`** is **`3.0.0`**. A **patch** bump from **`2.3.0`** is **`2.3.1`** (only **`C`** moves; there is no component to the right of **`C`** to zero).

If a single release mixes major, minor, and patch-style work, still apply **only** the **highest** applicable bump once (e.g. milestone + architecture → **`A`** only → **`3.0.0`** after **`2.x.y`**); do not stack multiple component bumps for the same release.

## Merge / PR checks

Before merging **incoming → base** (examples: `bug/*` → `develop`, `develop` → `main`):

1. Compare versions: use the **merge target** **`userland/shell/version_def.h`** (published from **`version/locked/`**) as the baseline **VERSION**.
2. On the **incoming** branch, ensure the new work is covered by **`version/entries/*.ver`** whose internal **MAJOR/STANDARD/RELEASE** (or the **highest** such triple among incoming entries) is **strictly greater** than the target **VERSION** when the PR introduces a new release. (If the PR also updates **`version/locked/`** through a maintainer finalize, you may compare incoming **`version_def.h`** to the target instead.)
3. If both show the **same** version (e.g. both `2.0.0`), **update the incoming branch** so its **entries** record a semver **one appropriate step ahead** of the target.

Example: `bug/…` → `develop`, both at **`2.0.0`** → bump incoming **entries** to **`2.0.1`** (patch for a bugfix branch).

When bumping, add or extend **`version/entries/*.ver`** (typically **one** new file per feature PR, revised in place). Pushing to **`develop`** runs **Version lock on merge** (**relocate** root **`PRERELEASE=1`** rows, entries → **`version/locked/`** without top-level **`preproduction */`**, refresh **`version_def.h`**, opens a PR when there are changes). **Maintainers** may run **`make finalize-version-locked`** locally before merge for an early **`version/locked/`** update on the branch. Do not merge with identical versions across branches when the change warrants a bump. Changelog assembly is **deployment-time**, not **`make`**.
